<title>POLAND: Handlowy falls for first time, seen up.</title>
<headline>Handlowy falls for first time, seen up.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Handlowy SA fell for the first time on Wednesday, after starting trade on Monday last week, down 2.1 percent to 42.5 zlotys in lower 15.9-million-zloty turnover.</p>
<p>Handlowy had opened 8.3 percent above issue at 37.9 zlotys.</p>
<p>Analysts said the strong buying after fixing signalled a rebound on Thursday but that the stock could soon level out.</p>
<p>&quot;Maybe the stock will stabilise because there's been a big exchange of shares at the current level which suggests the market for the stock reaching an equilibrium,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
